course: dictionary
lesson: 8650
title: A word for people who look hard
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A searcher is someone who looks hard for a lost person, animal or thing. You can work out the meaning from the clues in the sentence: «Searchers find a child who stays put much faster than one who keeps walking.» Searchers find a child, so they must be the people who look for him.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A searcher can also be a person or a program that looks for information. Try each meaning in the sentence and see which one makes sense.
explain: Safety lessons use this word to teach you what to do. «It is easier for searchers to find someone who stays in one place.» If you get lost, stay where you are so searchers can find you.
fact: A searcher is a person who looks hard for someone or something.
fact: Searchers often look for lost people, animals or things in forests, mountains or the sea.
fact: A team of searchers may work together, and volunteer searchers give their time to help.
fact: If you get lost, stay in one place so searchers can find you more easily.
fact: Bright colours make you easier for searchers to see.
exercise: What is a searcher? | A bird that sings at night | *A person who looks hard for someone or something | A kind of hot drink
exercise: «It is easier for searchers to find someone who stays in one place.» What should you do if you are lost? | *Stay in one place so searchers can find you | Run as fast as you can away from the path | Hide from everyone you see
exercise: Which phrase means people who give their time to help search? | Team of searchers | Searchers found | *Volunteer searchers
test: «A boy in Colorado left the trail in the woods to follow a deer; he got lost, and it took searchers all night to find him.» What happened after the boy left the trail? | He went to bed early | He found his way home at once | *He got lost, and searchers spent all night finding him | He became a searcher himself
test: If you are lost, which choice helps searchers most? | *Stay in one place and wait for searchers | Climb a tree and wait | Follow a deer through the woods | Keep walking to find help
exam: Which answer says what searchers do? | They hide from people | They write poems about the sea | They sell tickets at the station | *They look hard for lost people, animals or things
